Refiner (TRM-style recursive refinement, 1.8M params, matched compute) SOLVES
18.2% of Sudoku-Extreme exactly (blank-cell acc 0.652, 9.4 violations) — a +18pp
win over AR (greedy 0.002 / SC@32 0.000, blank-cell 0.342, 7.6 viol). The EBT is a
near-perfect energy SCORER (NCE loss 0.0001, gold-vs-corrupt gap 17) that FAILS to
GENERATE: both per-cell argmin and continuous energy-descent decode give 0.000
solve, 0.109 blank-cell (=chance), 132-145 violations (worse than random).

SYNTHESIS: VALIDATE the regime claim via REFINEMENT, REFUTE naive energy-descent.
On the weak-AR Sudoku regime a non-AR holistic generator beats AR — but the WINNER
is recursive refinement, NOT energy-descent. DT-P2 made concrete: refinement
(end-to-end vector field) generates; contrastive-energy-descent (curl-free scorer)
does not. Kona's 96% is plausibly refinement/amortized-inference, not naive
descent. For Carnot Phase-3: pursue recursive refinement as the generator
substrate; the energy function's role stays SCORING/verification (where the EBT is
near-perfect). Unlike P1's inconclusive arithmetic, this regime-corrected test is
decisive. Full artifact: results/experiment_sudoku_energy_vs_ar_v1.json.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
